*HEADING
Young's modulus of a 50 % austenite + 50 % martensite mixture (20MnCr5)
** Units: mm, s, tonne, N, MPa, mJ, C
** KM: f_M = 1 - exp(-0.01 (385 - T)) = 0.5 at T = 385 - ln 2 / 0.01 = 315.7 C.
** Quench 1000 -> 316 C at 1000 C/s (no ferrite or bainite), hold, then 10 MPa along z:
** E_mix = 10 / dE33, to compare with 0.5 E_A(316) + 0.5 E_M(316) of the card (rule of mixtures
** expected from the hierarchical interpolation in the ratios r2-r4).
